{
  "metadata" : [ {
    "label" : "Title",
    "value" : "Scop hwīlum sang "
  }, {
    "label" : "Author",
    "value" : "Jones, Shirley, 1934-"
  }, {
    "label" : "Subjects",
    "value" : "Aquatints -- specimens"
  }, {
    "label" : "Subjects",
    "value" : "Etchings -- specimens"
  }, {
    "label" : "Subjects",
    "value" : "Artists' books -- Wales"
  }, {
    "label" : "Description",
    "value" : "Scop hwīlum sang / Sometimes a poet sang is a suite of six etchings by Shirley Jones inspired by passages of Anglo Saxon poetry, hand-set and printed by her in 18-point Baskerville type, on Barcham Green hand-made paper. The first twenty five prints of an edition limited to fifty, appear along with the poems in bound books. White wove paper, etchings guarded by tissue. Bound by Mary French in quarter terracotta morocco and black linen, with illustration on front. Terracotta Fabriano Roma handmade laid endpapers, and binder's leaves inserted at front and back. Black linen drop-back box, with title on terracotta paper cover label. Inner tray lined with terracotta Fabriano Roma handmade laid papers. Copy 20/50, signed by Shirley Jones, dated 1983."
  }, {
    "label" : "Related Titles",
    "value" : "Artists' books:Collection"
  }, {
    "label" : "Publisher",
    "value" : "Brecon: Red Hen Press"
  }, {
    "label" : "Creation Date",
    "value" : "1983"
  }, {
    "label" : "Source",
    "value" : "alma"
  } ],
  "label" : "Scop hwīlum sang ",
  "description" : "Scop hwīlum sang / Sometimes a poet sang is a suite of six etchings by Shirley Jones inspired by passages of Anglo Saxon poetry, hand-set and printed by her in 18-point Baskerville type, on Barcham Green hand-made paper. The first twenty five prints of an edition limited to fifty, appear along with the poems in bound books. White wove paper, etchings guarded by tissue. Bound by Mary French in quarter terracotta morocco and black linen, with illustration on front. Terracotta Fabriano Roma handmade laid endpapers, and binder's leaves inserted at front and back. Black linen drop-back box, with title on terracotta paper cover label. Inner tray lined with terracotta Fabriano Roma handmade laid papers. Copy 20/50, signed by Shirley Jones, dated 1983.",
  "attribution" : "This title is licensed under <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\">CC BY 4.0. </a> Re-use must be attributed to Cardiff University Special Collections and Archives / Trwyddedwyd y teitl hwn o dan <a target=\"_blank\" href=https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0></a>CC BY 4.0. </a> Rhaid priodoli ail-ddefnydd i Gasgliadau Arbennig ac Archifau Prifysgol Caerdydd.",
